#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "fe2f3934-fa5c-5a59-be7e-00b6e4889063" :question/math-academy-id "e-4810" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/9832b17728be69381a5f534317c0f30156fd32f3706f4cd4634765a02370180e.png)" :question/worked-solution "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119551 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e38db5fa-1753-5176-bb5e-a077ea63ddec" :question/math-academy-id "e-4812" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/a8b13d238a1e77d90abe70a505c68a72060ea95fe545f56ae53e7cf40ba0595e.png) and the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/6e9f6c010c3137438923dfc32674dedf6d2d554b9b0a6745b007d826954d1e65.png) Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A),$ then we must have $A\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6+2k-12 \\\\ -6+3k-3 \\\\ 12-6k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ 3k-9=0 \\\\ -6k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "1e59cd29-ea54-5b90-8215-60c81d1b6dbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4814" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/787a2e53b8e39e79e0e4a2379082187a445a9c6babe0677fa315c516c01f0f67.png) Find $\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that $x_2=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3(0) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064430/assets/f73d7951a041c633d78d1d6971a3473800727452bb92e1b39ad574a045e1b76f.png) is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\right\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4ff2ede-223b-5edb-899d-9f9877cbd3c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348351} {:answer/id #uuid "5642ce81-e853-5332-85e5-c6be065d4ca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348352} {:answer/id #uuid "f121a408-cbe6-5444-b108-78ef55c66392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348353} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c7bdc7-e53e-5d94-be5b-ee30a1a059c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348354} {:answer/id #uuid "a2dd264a-796c-5e48-b7ea-df53dc192ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4ff2ede-223b-5edb-899d-9f9877cbd3c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348351} :answer-field/id #uuid "56bad962-017d-54ee-9bfc-d6fab9e2f83b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14aa32cf-8550-54fc-b750-a589ef676fd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-111079" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ lie in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb2e96e2-da62-5903-b3e0-a69acc1c4c5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348358} {:answer/id #uuid "7dab1407-7408-56a1-8d78-39e2b49774ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348359} {:answer/id #uuid "686e3339-8c57-5e60-aef0-80138037ee02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348360} {:answer/id #uuid "88f638b4-4824-52d0-ab2b-594d9009fd10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348361} {:answer/id #uuid "1af731e9-5c02-596e-a975-2c1841af3501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88f638b4-4824-52d0-ab2b-594d9009fd10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348361} :answer-field/id #uuid "351fd9fd-2830-5a89-b3ec-ebbf8d18c91c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03da8cae-b4ac-5129-bb9b-12c972f7230b" :question/math-academy-id "q-111091" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}39 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}34 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-33 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ef9699f-7560-56eb-9907-3ffd142c7e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348365} {:answer/id #uuid "2865b31b-8b43-5cf5-ad04-3c50b7776819" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348366} {:answer/id #uuid "e9548d61-cf9a-5d1d-9331-ad7ec21d7f15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348367} {:answer/id #uuid "497168b6-727c-54a0-937c-371bc2d17063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348368} {:answer/id #uuid "835ea043-16c1-5112-ad07-aa25afe78233" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ef9699f-7560-56eb-9907-3ffd142c7e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348365} :answer-field/id #uuid "590fdbea-7728-5d6b-a275-5660a8135471" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27e74dc5-1bf7-5c99-af0d-ca267a03f334" :question/math-academy-id "q-111109" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 15 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 15 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-5k+60 \\\\ k-12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5k+60=0 \\\\ k-12=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0c0a395-bd55-57e3-85d4-ab60cee68355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348372} {:answer/id #uuid "d5bbb0ce-a11f-52dd-bd59-fae6c1d45e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348373} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a3911a-dc28-5ebb-b537-b80bcf1b6111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348374} {:answer/id #uuid "a3710b05-1788-5033-bdee-89b311dc97bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348375} {:answer/id #uuid "12a75401-a3f6-5f3f-8809-5768728371e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5bbb0ce-a11f-52dd-bd59-fae6c1d45e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348373} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a1ae855-150d-5f5f-8cc8-ce70582a6f72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69e69f91-ec1e-542e-9931-23657109c1df" :question/math-academy-id "q-111112" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}28 & -7 & 14 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-7k+14 \\\\ k-2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-7k+14=0 \\\\ k-2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "013fca74-c93d-5f9a-b622-75e18c6e670b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348378} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd71ab1-7480-5dfc-837d-3ea7ddf44555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348379} {:answer/id #uuid "17c2eefb-f3ea-5112-8fdf-b0744079cbf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348380} {:answer/id #uuid "f53ab6fe-63d7-5f6d-a66f-2f12cb3f33e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348381} {:answer/id #uuid "fb23f712-a66c-540f-8f53-ea184c6a2b56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb23f712-a66c-540f-8f53-ea184c6a2b56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348382} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f73e1a5-c789-5447-8de5-7aaa900fe128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dcd84fb5-e504-5016-bbba-4d8edb437f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-34333" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e61b398-3098-5002-b813-6607183debfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348385} {:answer/id #uuid "c43b4a17-3d76-5fbf-b2a5-18418608b3be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348386} {:answer/id #uuid "28a46dfc-d92e-5450-9a26-1065cda04b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348387} {:answer/id #uuid "88e3a379-ebaf-5625-96cf-90a97fbae33a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348388} {:answer/id #uuid "594b06db-7e4d-576f-91ba-91c6cc56aee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -11{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88e3a379-ebaf-5625-96cf-90a97fbae33a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348388} :answer-field/id #uuid "410ee353-55e9-5f9c-b34e-3548f5a62c69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d54de9d5-0eaf-51ac-a971-a5633a39368a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34334" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variables, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}.$ Substituting ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(4{x}_{3})+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-11{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1e8f6c9-8a98-5c77-b6c7-c3442d33c006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348392} {:answer/id #uuid "c24e0f0c-b0db-598b-91e0-78fbf0be490a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348393} {:answer/id #uuid "c1151688-d971-52f7-b6a9-5497ec3ceefe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348394} {:answer/id #uuid "ea680adc-8692-5561-b18d-21e5e8775d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348395} {:answer/id #uuid "c69a15a7-166f-51ac-bca4-7dd29a5d3910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1e8f6c9-8a98-5c77-b6c7-c3442d33c006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348392} :answer-field/id #uuid "50e37186-a7e5-5c56-8774-c050741145c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cade4505-b877-5cb5-ae1c-bc1354365d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34361" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}41 \\\\ 82\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{2}$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfe1656-1a47-52d0-b070-846b08bae965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348399} {:answer/id #uuid "eac09cee-d903-5773-aaa9-5f3939a6c315" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348400} {:answer/id #uuid "086466e3-1e26-56cc-a31f-1c77d536ba70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348401} {:answer/id #uuid "02e02867-b62f-52cd-a766-36b6df11235d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348402} {:answer/id #uuid "316a380e-87eb-53ff-9282-502eb6be80fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02e02867-b62f-52cd-a766-36b6df11235d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348402} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f8664e9-e015-5a42-8862-702d0de1aac1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e020e6a-b449-5e4a-a844-714301abab08" :question/math-academy-id "q-34384" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-59 \\\\ 118 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vector lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91b60cb5-5872-5d0d-abf9-7b20e31af683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348406} {:answer/id #uuid "905c271f-2249-5f50-ab0c-57575c16271a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348407} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf0a191-90e7-50c2-bec2-801ced709643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348408} {:answer/id #uuid "ea555f13-26d2-56d3-b014-5002b627dbe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348409} {:answer/id #uuid "e69031cd-3426-57a1-acbe-bd889db33b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bf0a191-90e7-50c2-bec2-801ced709643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348408} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad1fb962-4f75-5343-8652-1e74fb6e7235" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d71acede-9d33-5ce8-9ea2-b8a49b7523dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-34947" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2k-8 \\\\ k+4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2k-8=0 \\\\ k+4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a39d581c-3b62-5c09-a732-56adb33a38d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118264} {:answer/id #uuid "aa532d54-2c1f-51c9-9517-830bddc998b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118265} {:answer/id #uuid "06bf2739-60b7-51ae-9729-f70be3d53515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118266} {:answer/id #uuid "34f3a46f-4953-5c1d-ba88-02625e10d02f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118267} {:answer/id #uuid "78df5c8e-55da-5783-918c-a76a576b4acb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa532d54-2c1f-51c9-9517-830bddc998b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118265} :answer-field/id #uuid "59b85dee-84eb-5f97-bd5f-0408e1a48598" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e07b6e6-db6e-581c-8777-d093455ecec5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34948" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -15 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3k-15 \\\\ -2+k-3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3k-15=0 \\\\ k-5=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46d0eeb5-f2af-5dea-b8f5-0685c033a445" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348412} {:answer/id #uuid "eb50163b-9d5d-5ef5-8e38-696c9a4d7bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348413} {:answer/id #uuid "99cf3227-1b59-53ed-8648-a6af860a94c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348414} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8cbca3-4beb-5ccf-8475-c08ae065e6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348415} {:answer/id #uuid "b04dabf1-9b07-5825-a502-057e052d9a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb50163b-9d5d-5ef5-8e38-696c9a4d7bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348413} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdc2298c-7547-509a-aafd-8ef518ce57cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c2b12c60-dc2b-5369-b49c-eb15948f4eb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-34951" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$  and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b16f743-bc51-5e6a-9646-075dfeed57b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348419} {:answer/id #uuid "133dec02-3553-5831-ae87-eaea2995b7eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$,  ${b}_{2}$, and ${b}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348420} {:answer/id #uuid "9355a77f-f7df-5c4f-99ce-71ee2b42a03d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348421} {:answer/id #uuid "f3811d06-576e-5c60-9f45-b0684c796920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348422} {:answer/id #uuid "b00fd5c9-6d88-5e3d-b841-813a8031a99d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9355a77f-f7df-5c4f-99ce-71ee2b42a03d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348421} :answer-field/id #uuid "a48c27d9-5ecc-5a81-87c5-ee76a24088e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65ef5949-cf70-59d8-adcb-422768352bc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34984" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-4\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=4\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{1}$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c140b910-0640-53ad-8bab-e3c4cd53e3f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348426} {:answer/id #uuid "7274b488-1c14-5dcc-9588-63866cdbf2c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348427} {:answer/id #uuid "5b517a9b-7e07-554f-9219-c82e72fc76f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348428} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0e871b-548a-5207-a133-52f7694a9e08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348429} {:answer/id #uuid "b2da721f-22ed-5d4c-9b7f-f75b469f3b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c140b910-0640-53ad-8bab-e3c4cd53e3f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348426} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfba941f-d34a-5aca-a48f-0f27cbecce4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b18bee2-485c-5ad8-a3de-5abedad9f1a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74867" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4k-8 \\\\ 2k-4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4k-8=0 \\\\ 2k-4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b51c632c-eee1-515a-bc97-2b6252853576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348433} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2b80fe-f939-58bb-9338-47ef09e9b1f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348434} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef04d45-055b-54ab-9fc6-64784f844547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348435} {:answer/id #uuid "539e6d1e-d394-5759-8ca2-7e0d84095f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348436} {:answer/id #uuid "1457ce0e-5a84-5bb5-81bd-e4323eb7d5eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ef04d45-055b-54ab-9fc6-64784f844547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348435} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1c4956-7a4b-5521-aeab-1a18c32218cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "352124af-7592-5133-a0e8-40dd6ba11465" :question/math-academy-id "q-74870" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$  and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348438 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70d2ab91-f71f-509e-8130-e1b9b95aa016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348440} {:answer/id #uuid "9e76bced-10a6-5e0c-8673-9b861562bf60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348441} {:answer/id #uuid "4a180622-23ec-50c0-8a59-b1ba3b941533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348442} {:answer/id #uuid "bc1a128d-3b94-5156-a770-06112ace0ddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348443} {:answer/id #uuid "961a0716-9c5e-5e4d-b1cf-8aea790908f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70d2ab91-f71f-509e-8130-e1b9b95aa016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348440} :answer-field/id #uuid "f384dc46-23e6-5c81-87c7-014cacbe321b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c1241fbe-f91a-51dc-8cf4-08074a70bd68" :question/math-academy-id "q-74872" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-3{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$"}]}
